        { name: "Homeowner-Frame Policy Defaults in a Majority-Renter District", tag: "avoid", why: "Applying a homeowner-first, property-rights frame to a district where 55.7% of households rent is a fundamental misread of who the constituency is. Policy positions that default to the interests and perspectives of property owners — on housing, taxation, and government services — will read as indifferent or hostile to the working families, renters, and minority communities who constitute the district's actual majority. The candidate who understands this district leads with the concerns of its actual residents rather than a generic rural-conservative script written for a different constituency." }
